<p>A <code>FiveFaceRatingPickerButton</code> is one face inside
  a <a href="/components/five-face-rating-picker/"><code>FiveFaceRatingPicker</code></a>.
  Each button is a <code>&lt;button role="radio"&gt;</code> with
  <code>data-value</code> (1–5). The example CSS renders an emoji
  per value: 😖 🙁 😐 🙂 😄.</p>

<p>See the <a href="/components/five-face-rating-picker/">Picker
  demo</a> for composed examples.</p>

{# BEGIN generated: examples (bin/generate-examples) #}
<h2>Usage</h2>
<pre tabindex="0"><code>{% raw %}&lt;FiveFaceRatingPicker label="How was your experience?"&gt;
    &lt;FiveFaceRatingPickerButton value="1" label="Very bad" onclick={handleClick} /&gt;
    &lt;FiveFaceRatingPickerButton value="2" label="Bad" onclick={handleClick} /&gt;
    &lt;FiveFaceRatingPickerButton value="3" label="Okay" onclick={handleClick} /&gt;
    &lt;FiveFaceRatingPickerButton value="4" label="Good" selected onclick={handleClick} /&gt;
    &lt;FiveFaceRatingPickerButton value="5" label="Very good" onclick={handleClick} /&gt;
&lt;/FiveFaceRatingPicker&gt;
{% endraw %}</code></pre>
